@host = http://localhost:5030

# Ready-to-run requests for VS Code (REST Client) and Rider. Send them from
# top to bottom: register a workspace first, then log in as its owner.

### Register a new workspace (201 + a token for its owner)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register-tenant
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantName": "Initech",
  "email": "owner@initech.example",
  "password": "Initech-Pass-2026"
}

### Log in as the owner of that workspace
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "owner@initech.example",
  "password": "Initech-Pass-2026"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Who am I
GET {{host}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Grant a permission (needs UsersManage, e.g. the owner; the body takes the number: 1 = UsersView)
# POST {{host}}/api/users/<userId>/permissions
# Authorization: Bearer <owner token>
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "permission": 1 }

### Revoke it (name or number)
# DELETE {{host}}/api/users/<userId>/permissions/UsersView
# Authorization: Bearer <owner token>


### Create a branch (OrganizationManage; the owner has it) - 201 + Location
# @name branch
POST {{host}}/api/branches
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sede Centro" }

###
@branchId = {{branch.response.body.id}}

### Create a WhatsApp channel - 201; the body has the webhookPath and the webhookSecret (shown only once)
POST {{host}}/api/channels
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "branchId": "{{branchId}}", "displayPhoneNumber": "+57 300 123 4567", "providerPhoneNumberId": null }

### Create an advisor
POST {{host}}/api/advisors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ana Pérez", "branchId": "{{branchId}}", "userId": null }

### List them (OrganizationView)
GET {{host}}/api/branches
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List conversations (ConversationsView), newest first. Filters: branchId, advisorId, unassigned, stage, source, status, from, to, unanswered (open and without a reply), closedUnanswered (closed and never replied)
GET {{host}}/api/conversations?pageSize=20&stage=InFollowUp
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One conversation with its messages
# GET {{host}}/api/conversations/<conversationId>
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Assign an advisor of the conversation's branch (ConversationsManage); { "advisorId": null } unassigns
# PUT {{host}}/api/conversations/<conversationId>/advisor
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "advisorId": "<advisorId>" }

### Decide the outcome by hand: Won, InFollowUp, or Lost with a lossReason (Unknown, Price, Availability, Location, Timing, Competitor, NoResponse, NotInterested, Other)
# PUT {{host}}/api/conversations/<conversationId>/opportunity
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "stage": "Lost", "lossReason": "Price", "detail": "Le pareció caro el paquete" }

### Deliver a 360dialog message to a channel (anonymous; the secret comes from the channel creation answer)
# Use the webhookPath and webhookSecret returned by POST /api/channels. Always answers 200 for a JSON object; the worker processes it a moment later.
# POST {{host}}/api/webhooks/360dialog/<channelKey>
# X-Webhook-Secret: <webhookSecret>
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "entry": [ { "changes": [ { "field": "messages", "value": {
#     "metadata": { "phone_number_id": "106540352242922" },
#     "contacts": [ { "profile": { "name": "Laura" }, "wa_id": "573005550101" } ],
#     "messages": [ { "from": "573005550101", "id": "wamid.TEST-1", "timestamp": "1792324800", "type": "text", "text": { "body": "Hola" } } ]
# } } ] } ] }
